ublish a file. A file attached to a Public post is readable through that post by anyone. Members posts are readable by signed-in members.</p><p>Reuse a file in multiple posts. Remove all references before deleting the file. Copies that others have downloaded cannot be recalled.</p><h2>Storage</h2><p>Upload up to 256 MiB per file, with 2 GiB of storage per account. Originals are preserved. Location metadata is not removed; files are not compressed or transcoded.</p><p>Data history and operational backups may remain. Deleting an item does not guarantee physical erasure from every retained copy.</p><h2>Account</h2><p>There is no email-based password recovery. Keep your password somewhere safe. An administrator's invitation is required to create an account.</p><p class=\"field-help\">Built with lkjscript.</p></section>")) (text "") (text "")) (if (call std::text-equal (field (local request) (name path)) (text "/media")) (call delivery::file (local ctx) (local request)) (if (call std::text-equal (field (local request) (name path)) (text "/healthz")) (call health::respond (local request)) (call page::error (i64 404) (text "Page not found."))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))

